From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dreyk <dreyksmail@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:37:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] wifi: mt76: mt76x2e: restart mac_work after a channel
 change

mt76_set_channel() cancels phy->mac_work before calling drv->set_channel()
(since openwrt/mt76 commit b80c997b3f, mainline Linux f4fdd7716290,
"wifi: mt76: partially move channel change code to core").
mt7603_set_channel() re-queues mac_work at the end, whereas
mt76x2e_set_channel() does not. Because mac80211 changes the channel
immediately after drv_start() and again when the AP starts, phy1's
mt76x02_mac_work() stops permanently and never runs while the AP is up.

Without mt76x02_mac_work(), the 5 GHz radio loses periodic survey
updates, A-MPDU aggregation counters (ampdu_stat), MAC beacon-hang
recovery (mt76x02_check_mac_err()), ED/CCA monitoring, and periodic
cleanup of stale TX status entries (mt76_tx_status_check()).

Re-queue phy->mac_work at MT_MAC_WORK_INTERVAL (100 ms) at the end of
mt76x2e_set_channel() when MT76_STATE_RUNNING is set. All stop paths
clear MT76_STATE_RUNNING before cancelling mac_work, and mac80211 calls
config() only while open, so guarding with MT76_STATE_RUNNING avoids
arming mac_work if set_channel is ever invoked while the device is
stopped.
---
 mt76x2/pci_main.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mt76x2/pci_main.c b/mt76x2/pci_main.c
index cd813079..5e3a4f25 100644
--- a/mt76x2/pci_main.c
+++ b/mt76x2/pci_main.c
@@ -50,6 +50,10 @@ int mt76x2e_set_channel(struct mt76_phy *phy)
 	tasklet_enable(&dev->dfs_pd.dfs_tasklet);
 	tasklet_enable(&dev->mt76.pre_tbtt_tasklet);
 
+	if (test_bit(MT76_STATE_RUNNING, &phy->state))
+		ieee80211_queue_delayed_work(mt76_hw(dev), &phy->mac_work,
+					     MT_MAC_WORK_INTERVAL);
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
